  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID&apos;s Youth Entrepreneurship and Empowerment Support (YES) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID Youth Entrepreneurship and Empowerment Support (YES) activity addresses drivers of conflict stemming from the influx of Rohingya refugees in Cox&apos;s Bazar area.  One of the main objectives of the YES activity is to increase market-oriented vocational skills for in-school and out-of-school youths.  The training curricula is created to provide youths with leadership, soft skills, and promote social cohesion.  The activity is specifically designed to target unemployed, unskilled, illiterate and out of school youth, with special focus on female youth.  With FY 2021 funds, USAID will enhance the capacity of local actors, such as civil society organizations, local businesses and local government agencies, with the goal of developing social and economic resilience in host communities.  USAID will build partnerships with local businesses to connect trained youths with employers through job fairs, internships, and apprenticeships.  It will link beneficiaries to financing opportunities to encourage youth entrepreneurs.  With the FY 2021 fund, this activity will also support efforts to counter violent extremism by teaching youths positive-coping techniques and conflict mitigation skills.  This IM meet $400K of the DRG earmarks..This activity will be in line with the State-USAID Integrated Country Strategy (ICS) Mission Goals One and Two and the U.S. government development objective of strengthened resilience to shocks and stressors..</narrative>
  </description>
